Australia is a federation comprising six states and two major mainland territories. Unlike many countries, Australia does not have a single "capital city" in the traditional sense because its federal capital territory (the Australian Capital Territory or ACT) contains the national capital city.

The city located within this federal capital territory is **Canberra**. Although Canberra was designed to compromise between Sydney and Melbourne (both claimants to being the nation's first major cities), it serves as the administrative capital of Australia.

